            <ArticleTitle>Use of the exercise test in the diagnosis of coronary disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The two-step test remains a useful office procedure for the diagnosis of serious coronary disease. The graded exercise test has improved sensitivity. Requiring a good performance and a normal electrocardiographic response as well can exclude prognostically important disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
